% ============================================================================
% references.bib -- MSSP draft
%
% AUDITED 11 Aug 2026. All 35 entries were checked by resolving each claimed
% title against an authoritative record (Crossref, JMLR, arXiv, dblp, ISO),
% which is the only check that catches the failure mode where a real,
% resolvable DOI belongs to a DIFFERENT work than the one cited.
%
% Every entry carries a VERIFIED note naming the registry it was confirmed
% against. Entries with no DOI say why the venue mints none and where the
% metadata was confirmed instead. An entry with neither has not been audited
% -- treat that as a defect.
%
% Three near-miss traps found during the audit are recorded above
% casdagli1991, bishop1994 and wang2026fleet: in each case a real DOI exists
% for a same- or similar-titled work that is NOT the one cited.
%
% One substantive correction: nguyen2025subdomain named the wrong journal.
%
% 42 entries as of 11 Aug 2026, and all 42 are cited: the seven added after
% the audit (mackay2005dimension, bourlard1988, baldi1989, gong2019memae,
% grenander1994, cohen2016group, higgins2018) now carry the prose written for
% them, and levina2004 -- previously in the file but cited nowhere -- is used
% in three places. Checked both directions: no entry is uncited and no
% citation lacks an entry.
%
% FORMATTING RULE -- do not break this. Every comment in this file sits
% BETWEEN entries, never inside one. BibTeX does not treat '%' as a comment
% character inside an entry body: it reports "You're missing a field name" and
% then SILENTLY DISCARDS THE REST OF THE ENTRY. That surfaces as warnings in
% the .blg, not as errors, so the document still compiles and the reference
% prints with its author, title and journal missing. An earlier revision of
% this file lost six entries that way.
%
% Second rule from the same family: never write a bare at-sign in a comment.
% BibTeX scans for at-signs everywhere, comments included, and will try to
% parse what follows as an entry.
% ============================================================================

